 "_doc": "W6b monster frames: 128-unit frames, 2 units = 1 world px, facing right. Each kind has one anchor (its feet, or its middle for fliers), drip_hang included. Offsets from the anchor in world px = (point - anchor) / 2.",
 "_drip_hang": {
  "ceiling": [
   64,
   10
  ],
  "how": "drip_hang keeps the feet anchor (64, 122); its ceiling line is frame y 10. While hanging (position.y = the ceiling line), set sprite.position.y = 56 ((122 - 10) / 2) so frame y 10 sits on the ceiling; set it back to 0 when it lets go. Or write sprite.offset.y = -20 while hanging and -244 after. Do not change anchor at runtime: enemy.gd applies it to sprite.offset only in _ready.",
  "sprite_position_y": 56.0
 },
